      </section>

      <!-- ======================= 04 COMPONENTS ========================= -->
      <section id="components" class="guide-chapter" aria-labelledby="components-title">
        <header>
          <div><p class="prism-eyebrow">04 / Components</p><h2 id="components-title">The rules become a family.</h2></div>
          <p>Choose density, then role, then size. Every specimen shares one edge, one cast, and one light.</p>
        </header>

        <section class="ds-section" aria-labelledby="ds-density">
          <header>
            <span class="ds-law">LAW 5 · DENSITY</span>
            <h3 id="ds-density">Permanence condenses light into pigment</h3>
            <p>Move the light behind each card and compare the shadows. Destructive actions belong to the immovable tier.</p>
          </header>
          <div class="ds-grid ds-grid--3">
            <div class="prism-card ds-lift" data-light="transient">
              <p class="prism-eyebrow">Transient · T 0.6</p>
              <p class="prism-body" style="color: var(--ink-soft); margin: 0.4rem 0 1rem;">Seconds. Edge and glow; most light passes.</p>
              <button class="prism-btn prism-btn--primary prism-edge" type="button">Primary action</button>
            </div>
            <div class="prism-card" data-light="standing" style="border: 1px solid var(--hairline); background: var(--standing-tint); color: var(--on-ground); box-shadow: var(--elev-dense);">
              <p class="prism-eyebrow">Standing · T 0.3</p>
              <p class="prism-body" style="margin: 0.4rem 0 1rem;">Session. Tinted wash, 1px border, short shadow.</p>
              <button class="prism-btn" type="button" style="box-shadow: var(--elev-dense);">Secondary</button>
            </div>
            <div class="prism-card" data-light="immovable" style="background: var(--dense); color: var(--on-dense); box-shadow: var(--elev-dense);">
              <p class="prism-eyebrow">Immovable · T 0.05</p>
              <p class="prism-body" style="opacity: 0.85; margin: 0.4rem 0 1rem;">Structure. Opaque pigment, no spectra.</p>
              <div class="ds-row-actions">
                <button class="prism-btn prism-btn--dense" type="button">Save</button>
                <button class="prism-btn prism-btn--dense prism-btn--danger" type="button">Delete</button>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section class="ds-section" aria-labelledby="ds-matrix">
          <header>
            <span class="ds-law">SIZES × STYLES</span>
            <h3 id="ds-matrix">The set, laid out</h3>
            <p>Five sizes over four button styles, and three sizes over badges and chips. Drag the hue: brand styles rotate, semantics hold.</p>
          </header>
          <div class="prism-card" style="box-shadow: var(--elev-dense);">
            <p class="prism-eyebrow">Button · 5 sizes / 4 styles</p>
            <div class="ds-matrix" style="margin-top: 1rem;">
              <span class="ds-mx-label"></span>
              {['xs', 'sm', 'md', 'lg', 'xl'].map((n) => <span class="ds-mx-label">{n}</span>)}
              {[
                ['primary', 'prism-btn--primary prism-edge'],
                ['secondary', ''],
                ['dense', 'prism-btn--dense'],
                ['danger', 'prism-btn--dense prism-btn--danger'],
              ].map(([label, style]) => (
                <>
                  <span class="ds-mx-label">{label}</span>
                  {['prism-btn--xs', 'prism-btn--sm', '', 'prism-btn--lg', 'prism-btn--xl'].map((size) => (
                    <span class="ds-mx-cell"><button class={`prism-btn ${style} ${size}`} type="button">Deploy</button></span>
                  ))}
                </>
              ))}
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="prism-card" style="box-shadow: var(--elev-dense); margin-top: 1rem;">
            <p class="prism-eyebrow">Badge &amp; chip · 3 sizes</p>
            <div class="ds-stack" style="margin-top: 1rem; gap: 0.9rem;">
              {['sm', 'md', 'lg'].map((n) => (
                <div class="ds-row-actions">
                  <span class={`prism-badge prism-badge--ok prism-badge--${n}`}>✓ Approved</span>
                  <span class={`prism-badge prism-badge--no prism-badge--${n}`}>✕ Rejected</span>
                  <span class={`prism-badge prism-badge--warn prism-badge--${n}`}>! Pending</span>
                  <span class={`prism-chip prism-edge prism-chip--${n}`}><i class="prism-dot"></i>anchor</span>
                  <span class={`prism-chip prism-edge prism-chip--${n}`}>q = 40ms</span>
                  <span class="ds-mx-label">{n}</span>
                </div>
              ))}
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section class="ds-section" aria-labelledby="ds-displays">
          <header>
            <span class="ds-law">LAW 22 · ICONS &amp; DISPLAYS</span>
            <h3 id="ds-displays">Quantized light on tiny screens</h3>
            <p>
              After Ink &amp; Switch's <a href="https://www.inkandswitch.com/project/tenfold/playground/">Tenfold</a>:
              icons are 8×8 displays that emit rather than print, so the glass stays dark in both modes.
              Click an icon to re-tune its band. Drag on the large display to paint.
            </p>
          </header>
          <div class="ds-grid ds-grid--2" style="align-items: start;">
            <div class="ds-icon-row" aria-label="Icon displays">
              {glyphs.map((g) => (
                <button class="ds-icon-tile" type="button" data-cycle data-name={g.name} aria-label={`${g.name} display — band anchor, click to re-tune`}>
                  <span class="prism-screen" data-band="anchor" aria-hidden="true">
                    {g.rows.join('').split('').map((c) => <b class={c === '#' ? 'on' : undefined}></b>)}
                  </span>
                  <span class="prism-data">{g.name}</span>
                </button>
              ))}
            </div>
            <div>
              <div
                id="ds-paint"
                class="prism-screen ds-paint"
