          </div>
        </section>
      </section>

      <!-- =================== 05 INFORMATION PATTERNS =================== -->
      <section id="information" class="guide-chapter" aria-labelledby="information-title">
        <header>
          <div><p class="prism-eyebrow">05 / Information patterns</p><h2 id="information-title">Give light a reading order.</h2></div>
          <p>Summarize before showing evidence, and keep selection separate from status. As density rises, hairlines replace light.</p>
        </header>
        <div class="guide-composition">
          <div class="prism-card prism-edge">
            <p class="prism-eyebrow">Pattern / summary</p>
            <h3>One release needs attention.</h3>
            <p>Two checks are ready. One needs a decision.</p>
            <p style="margin-top: 1.2rem;"><span class="prism-badge prism-badge--warn">! Review required</span></p>
            <p class="ds-caption">The summary floats above the records, and its status is named in words.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="guide-table-wrap">
            <table class="guide-table">
              <caption>Pattern / comparison and decision</caption>
              <thead><tr><th scope="col">Check</th><th scope="col">Result</th><th scope="col">Next step</th></tr></thead>
              <tbody>
                <tr class="guide-record"><th scope="row">Typography</th><td>✓ Ready</td><td>Keep scale</td></tr>
                <tr class="guide-record" data-current="true"><th scope="row">Focus states<small>Current review</small></th><td>! Review</td><td>Inspect ring</td></tr>
                <tr class="guide-record"><th scope="row">Motion</th><td>✓ Ready</td><td>Keep timing</td></tr>
              </tbody>
            </table>
          </div>
        </div>

        <section class="ds-section" aria-labelledby="ds-elevation">
          <header>
            <span class="ds-law">LAW 6–7 · ELEVATION</span>
            <h3 id="ds-elevation">Casts float; hairlines ground</h3>
            <p>
              Day casts fall away from the pointer; night casts become halos. Data rows never cast.
              Selection enters as a 2px seam, and a shared datum lights everywhere at once (Δt = 0).
            </p>
          </header>
          <div class="ds-grid ds-grid--2" style="align-items: start;">
            <div class="prism-card ds-lift prism-edge">
              <p class="prism-eyebrow">Floating card · entangled</p>
              <p class="prism-body" style="margin: 0.5rem 0 1rem; color: var(--ink-soft);">Hover a dot or a row. Both light at once; their neighbors stay put.</p>
              <div class="ds-row-actions" style="gap: 1.25rem;">
                <span class="prism-dot" data-pair="r1" tabindex="0" aria-label="datum 0xA1"></span>
                <span class="prism-dot" data-pair="r2" tabindex="0" aria-label="datum 0xA2"></span>
                <span class="prism-dot" data-pair="r3" tabindex="0" aria-label="datum 0xA3"></span>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="prism-table" role="table" aria-label="Dense data (hairline elevation)" style="--cols: 1fr 1fr 1fr;">
              <div class="ds-thead" role="row"><span role="columnheader">Run</span><span role="columnheader">Hue</span><span role="columnheader">State</span></div>
              <div class="prism-row" role="row" tabindex="0" data-pair="r1"><span>0xA1</span><span>185°</span><span>ok</span></div>
              <div class="prism-row" role="row" tabindex="0" data-pair="r2" aria-selected="true"><span>0xA2</span><span>150°</span><span>ok</span></div>
              <div class="prism-row" role="row" tabindex="0" data-pair="r3"><span>0xA3</span><span>027°</span><span>fail</span></div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>
      </section>

      <!-- ======================= 06 BUILD WITH IT ====================== -->
      <section id="use" class="guide-chapter" aria-labelledby="use-title">
        <header>
          <div><p class="prism-eyebrow">06 / Build with it</p><h2 id="use-title">A recipe, with boundaries.</h2></div>
          <p>Build from the material classes, keep the model visible in each choice, and verify the composition.</p>
        </header>
        <div class="ds-grid ds-grid--2">
          <div>
            <h3>Load the material, then the light.</h3>
            <pre class="guide-code" tabindex="0" aria-label="Prismatic starter markup"><code>{`<html data-mode="day" style="--h:185; --hr:129">
<link rel="stylesheet" href="/prism/prism.css">
<script type="module" src="/prism/light.js"></script>

<article class="prism-card prism-edge">
  <h2>Review the release</h2>
  <button class="prism-btn prism-btn--dense">
    Inspect release
  </button>
</article>
</html>`}</code></pre>
            <p>prism.css is the resting material. light.js is optional. It solves the field and writes the light refs, and it reads density from <code class="prism-data">data-light</code>. A hue control must also set <code class="prism-data">--hr</code>.</p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3>Know what to avoid.</h3>
            <ul class="guide-avoid">
              <li><strong>Independent colors</strong><p>Derive brand bands from the anchor and keep semantic hues fixed.</p></li>
              <li><strong>Glow on every row</strong><p>Dense data needs hairlines and a narrow seam.</p></li>
              <li><strong>Every object floats</strong><p>Density separates the temporary from the structural.</p></li>
              <li><strong>Color as the only message</strong><p>Keep labels, visible focus, and a reduced-motion path.</p></li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="ds-row-actions" style="margin-top: 1.5rem;">
          <a href="/prism/prism.tokens.json" download>Tokens ↓</a>
          <a href="/prism/prism.css" download>Material ↓</a>
          <a href="/prism/light.js" download>Light ↓</a>
          <a href="/design/void">Read VOID ↗</a>
          <a href="/design/acrylics">Read Acrylics ↗</a>
        </div>
      </section>
    </main>

    <footer class="ds-footer">
      <p>
        PRISM v0.8 · all color OKLCH · light by radiance cascades (<a href="https://radiance.wiki/">radiance.wiki</a>) ·
        <a href="/prism/prism.tokens.json">tokens</a> · <a href="/prism/prism.css">prism.css</a> · <a href="/prism/light.js">light.js</a>
      </p>
      <p>
        Contrast audit (WCAG AA): <code>scripts/prism-contrast-audit.mjs</code> checks the body-text pairs at hues
        <code>{`{20, 60, 90, 150, 185, 260, 310}`}</code> in both modes. It also checks text on the field under the
        light at its worst: a full-depth day shadow (≥ 8.1:1) and a full night glow (≥ 5.6:1). The 60–90° band is the
        known risk zone, and it passes.
      </p>
    </footer>

    <script is:inline>
      (function () {
        const root = document.documentElement;
        const slider = document.getElementById('ds-hue-slider');
        const modeBtn = document.getElementById('ds-mode-toggle');

        // Redshift: an art-directed hue map. Spectral hues (45–300) slide toward
        // red; non-spectral pinks (300–360) wrap forward.
        function prismRedshift(h, k = 0.4) {
          if (h <= 45) return h;
          if (h > 300) return Math.round((h + (385 - h) * k) % 360);
          return Math.round(h - (h - 45) * k);
        }

        function applyHue(h) {
          const hr = prismRedshift(h);
          root.style.setProperty('--h', h);
          root.style.setProperty('--hr', hr);
          document.getElementById('ds-day-h').textContent = h + '°';
          document.getElementById('ds-night-h').textContent = hr + '°';
          const night = root.dataset.mode === 'night';
          const offsets = night ? [0, -25, 55, -95] : [0, -35, 75, -140];
          const base = night ? hr : h;
          const bands = offsets.map((o) => ((base + o) % 360 + 360) % 360);
          document.getElementById('guide-hue-equation').textContent =
            (night ? 'Night' : 'Day') + ': H = ' + base + '° → bands ' + bands.map((b) => b + '°').join(', ');
          document.querySelectorAll('[data-band-offset]').forEach((label) => {
            const o = offsets[Number(label.dataset.bandOffset)];
            label.textContent = (o >= 0 ? '+' : '−') + Math.abs(o) + '°';
          });
        }
        slider.addEventListener('input', (e) => applyHue(parseInt(e.target.value, 10)));
        applyHue(parseInt(slider.value, 10));

        // Mode toggle — refracts over 25q; never snaps.
        modeBtn.addEventListener('click', () => {
          const next = root.dataset.mode === 'night' ? 'day' : 'night';
          root.dataset.mode = next;
          document.getElementById('ds-mode-label').textContent = next === 'night' ? 'Redshift' : 'Day';
          modeBtn.setAttribute('aria-pressed', String(next === 'night'));
          applyHue(parseInt(slider.value, 10));
        });

        // Replays: re-trigger an entrance by reflow.
        function restart(el, cls) {
          el.classList.remove(cls);
          void el.offsetWidth;
          el.classList.add(cls);
        }
        const ghosts = document.querySelectorAll('[data-ghost]');
        let collapsed = false;
        document.querySelectorAll('[data-replay]').forEach((btn) => {
          btn.addEventListener('click', () => {
            const kind = btn.dataset.replay;
            if (kind === 'stagger') restart(document.getElementById('ds-stagger'), 'prism-stagger');
            if (kind === 'enter') restart(document.getElementById('ds-enter').firstElementChild, 'prism-enter');
            if (kind === 'collapse') {
              collapsed = !collapsed;
              ghosts.forEach((g) => g.classList.toggle('collapsed', collapsed));
              document.getElementById('ds-collapsed').hidden = !collapsed;
              btn.textContent = collapsed ? 'Superpose' : 'Observe';
            }
          });
        });

        // Entanglement: everything sharing a datum lights with Δt = 0.
        document.querySelectorAll('[data-pair]').forEach((el) => {
          const lit = (on) => document.querySelectorAll('[data-pair="' + el.dataset.pair + '"]')
            .forEach((n) => n.classList.toggle('lit', on));
          el.addEventListener('mouseenter', () => lit(true));
          el.addEventListener('mouseleave', () => lit(false));
          el.addEventListener('focus', () => lit(true));
          el.addEventListener('blur', () => lit(false));
        });

        // Icons: click to re-tune a display's emission band.
        const bands = ['anchor', 'near', 'far', 'counter'];
        document.querySelectorAll('[data-cycle]').forEach((btn) => {
          btn.addEventListener('click', () => {
            const screen = btn.querySelector('.prism-screen');
            const band = bands[(bands.indexOf(screen.dataset.band) + 1) % bands.length];
            screen.dataset.band = band;
            btn.setAttribute('aria-label', btn.dataset.name + ' display — band ' + band + ', click to re-tune');
          });
        });

        // Paint display — click and drag everywhere (after Tenfold).
        const paint = document.getElementById('ds-paint');
        const cells = Array.from(paint.children);
        const COLS = 16, ROWS = 10;
        let painting = false, paintOn = true, cur = 0;
        function cellAt(e) {
          const c0 = cells[0].getBoundingClientRect();
          const col = Math.floor((e.clientX - c0.left) / (cells[1].getBoundingClientRect().left - c0.left));
          const row = Math.floor((e.clientY - c0.top) / (cells[COLS].getBoundingClientRect().top - c0.top));
          return col < 0 || col >= COLS || row < 0 || row >= ROWS ? null : cells[row * COLS + col];
        }
        paint.addEventListener('pointerdown', (e) => {
          const c = cellAt(e);
          if (!c) return;
          painting = true;
          paintOn = !c.classList.contains('on');
          c.classList.toggle('on', paintOn);
          paint.setPointerCapture(e.pointerId);
          e.preventDefault();
        });
        paint.addEventListener('pointermove', (e) => {
          const c = painting && cellAt(e);
          if (c) c.classList.toggle('on', paintOn);
        });
        ['pointerup', 'pointercancel'].forEach((t) => paint.addEventListener(t, () => { painting = false; }));
        paint.addEventListener('keydown', (e) => {
          const step = { ArrowLeft: -1, ArrowRight: 1, ArrowUp: -COLS, ArrowDown: COLS }[e.key];
          if (step !== undefined) {
            cells[cur].classList.remove('cursor');
            cur = Math.max(0, Math.min(cells.length - 1, cur + step));
            cells[cur].classList.add('cursor');
            e.preventDefault();
          } else if (e.key === 'Enter' || e.key === ' ') {
            cells[cur].classList.toggle('on');
            e.preventDefault();
          }
        });
        paint.addEventListener('focus', () => cells[cur].classList.add('cursor'));
        paint.addEventListener('blur', () => cells[cur].classList.remove('cursor'));
        document.getElementById('ds-paint-clear').addEventListener('click', () => cells.forEach((c) => c.classList.remove('on')));
      })();
    </script>

    <!-- The light: radiance field + reference beam, and its live monitor. -->
    <script type="module" is:inline>
      import { light } from '/prism/light.js';

      const $ = (id) => document.getElementById(id);
      const input = $('ds-cascades');
      let shape = '';

      input.addEventListener('input', () => light.setCascades(Number(input.value)));

      light.subscribe((l) => {
        $('ds-f-solves').textContent = l.solves;
        $('ds-f-frames').textContent = l.frames;
        $('ds-f-writes').textContent = l.writes;
        if (!l.radiant) return;
        const next = [l.field.join('×'), l.scale, l.maxCascades, l.cascades].join('|');
        if (next === shape) return;
        shape = next;
        $('ds-f-field').textContent = l.field.join(' × ');
        $('ds-f-texel').textContent = l.scale.toFixed(1);
        $('ds-f-status').textContent = 'WebGL2 · RGBA16F · direction-first layout · two solves per update.';
        $('ds-cascade-caption').textContent = 'Cascades at ' + innerWidth + ' × ' + innerHeight;
        input.disabled = false;
        input.max = String(l.maxCascades);
        input.value = String(l.cascades);
        $('ds-cascades-out').textContent = l.cascades;
        $('ds-cascade-rows').replaceChildren(...Array.from({ length: l.maxCascades }, (_, n) => {
          const tr = document.createElement('tr');
          if (n >= l.cascades) tr.dataset.off = '';
          const a = Math.round(l.l0 * (4 ** n - 1) / 3 * l.scale);
          const b = Math.round(l.l0 * (4 ** (n + 1) - 1) / 3 * l.scale);
          [n, (2 ** n * l.scale).toFixed(1) + ' px', (4 ** (n + 1)).toLocaleString('en-US'), a + '–' + b + ' px']
            .forEach((v) => tr.appendChild(document.createElement('td')).append(String(v)));
          return tr;
        }));
      });
    </script>
  </body>
</html>
